
#  What is a Matrix
   A matrix is just a grid of numbers — rows and columns.
   In Java, it's a 2D array: int[][] mat = new int[3][4];
   means 3 rows, 4 columns.

   int[][] mat = {
       {1, 2, 3},
       {4, 5, 6},
       {7, 8, 9}
   };
   // mat[0][0] = 1  → row 0, col 0
   // mat[1][2] = 6  → row 1, col 2
   // mat.length      = number of rows (3)
   // mat[0].length   = number of columns (3)

   mat[row][col] — row comes first, then column.
   Row = which line (vertical position),
   Col = which item in that line (horizontal position).

   How to loop through it (memorize this, you'll type it 100 times):

   for (int r = 0; r < mat.length; r++) {
       for (int c = 0; c < mat[0].length; c++) {
           System.out.print(mat[r][c] + " ");
       }
   }

   //Print a matrix row by row
   for (int r = 0; r < mat.length; r++) {        // outer loop = which row
               for (int c = 0; c < mat[0].length; c++) {  // inner loop = which column in that row
                   System.out.print(mat[r][c] + " ");
               }
               System.out.println(); // move to next line after finishing a row
           }
  // print a matrix col by col
     for (int c=0; c<mat[0].length ;c++){
             for(int r=0; r< mat.length; r++){
               System.out.print( mat[r][c]+" ");
             }
             System.out.println();
           }

  // Find sum of all elements
     int sum =0;
     for (int r = 0; r < mat.length; r++) {        // outer loop = which row
         for (int c = 0; c < mat[0].length; c++) {  // inner loop = which column in that row
             sum+=mat[r][c];
         }
         System.out.println(sum); // move to next line after finishing a row
     }

  // Find the max element and its position
      int max=mat [0][0];
           int maxRow=0;
             int maxCol=0;
           for (int r=0; r<mat.length ;r++){
             for(int c=0; c< mat[0].length; c++){
              if(mat[r][c]>max){
                max=mat[r][c];
                maxRow=r;
                maxCol=c;
              }
             }
           }
          System.out.println("Max = " + max + " at position (" + maxRow + ", " + maxCol + ")");

